Analyze Jira ticket [JIRA-KEY] and calculate the acknowledgement time and resolution time specifically for our team, [TEAM NAME].

Review the complete Jira history, including:
- Ticket creation timestamp
- Assignee changes
- Status transitions
- Comments and their authors
- Resolution timestamp
- Reopen events, if any

Definitions:

1. Acknowledgement time
The time between ticket creation and the first meaningful action from our team.

Count any of the following as acknowledgement:
- A team member posts a meaningful comment
- A team member accepts or assigns the ticket
- A team member moves the ticket into an active status such as Acknowledged, Assigned, In Progress, Investigation, or equivalent

Do not count:
- Automated notifications
- Bot-generated comments
- System-generated history updates
- Comments from the reporter, requester, or another support team
- Assignment to a queue without any action by our team

2. Resolution time
The time between ticket creation and the first valid transition to Resolved, Closed, Done, or the equivalent final status.

If the ticket was reopened:
- Show each resolution cycle separately
- Calculate the final resolution time up to the latest valid closure
- Clearly identify time spent in reopened status

3. Our team
Only consider actions performed by:
[ADD TEAM MEMBERS, JIRA GROUP, OR SUPPORT QUEUE]

Provide the results in this format:

| Metric | Start timestamp | End timestamp | Duration | Evidence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| First acknowledgement | Ticket created | First qualifying team action | Hours and minutes | Person, action/comment, and timestamp |
| First resolution | Ticket created | First resolved transition | Days, hours, and minutes | Status transition and timestamp |
| Final resolution | Ticket created | Latest valid closure | Days, hours, and minutes | Status transition and timestamp |

Also provide:
- Calendar-time duration
- Business-hours duration using [TIME ZONE], [WORKING HOURS], Monday–Friday, excluding weekends and configured holidays
- Current ticket status
- Current assignee
- A short chronological timeline of the important actions
- Whether the acknowledgement and resolution SLA were met, using these targets:
  - Acknowledgement SLA: [X HOURS]
  - Resolution SLA: [Y HOURS/DAYS]

Important rules:
- Use exact Jira timestamps and history as evidence.
- Do not estimate or assume missing information.
- Clearly state “Cannot determine from Jira history” if evidence is unavailable.
- Separate our team’s response from actions taken by other teams.
- If ownership was transferred to our team later, show both:
  1. Duration from ticket creation
  2. Duration from the time our team received ownership
- Include a direct link to the Jira ticket.
